course: dictionary
lesson: 668
title: Words for places where things are made and sold
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bakery is a shop where bread, cakes, buns and pies are baked and sold. The word comes from bake, which means to cook something in an oven, so a bakery is the place where baking happens.
explain: «La boulangerie is the bakery; the baker is le boulanger or la boulangère, and many French people buy fresh bread every day.» The sentence says people buy fresh bread there, so a bakery must be a shop. Try it: swap in «shop» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Bakery can also mean the place or factory where bread is baked. «Banks lend to help people buy homes and start businesses, like Ruby's aunt opening a bakery.» Here a bakery is a business, a place where bread and cakes are made and sold to customers.
fact: A bakery is a shop or business where bread, cakes, buns and pies are baked and sold.
fact: The plural of bakery is bakeries.
fact: «La boulangerie» is the French word for bakery, and «le boulanger» means the baker.
fact: Yeast makes bread rise, so bakers use it when they make bread.
fact: Opening a bakery is a business, and banks may lend money to help people start one, but they check the borrower can pay it back.
exercise: «La boulangerie» is the French word for bakery. What is a bakery? | A farm where wheat grows | A place to park your bike | *A shop where bread, cakes and buns are baked and sold
exercise: «Ruby's aunt is opening a bakery.» What does bakery mean in this sentence? | A field full of grain | A bank that lends money to people | *A business that bakes and sells bread and cakes
exercise: Which of these would you most likely buy at a bakery? | Bicycles | Garden hoses | *Fresh buns and pies
test: In a bakery, what does yeast do to the bread? | Makes it freeze | *Makes it rise | Turns it blue | Makes it shrink
test: What is the plural of bakery? | bakeree | bakerys | *bakeries | bakerie
exam: Why do banks check that a person can pay back a loan for a bakery? | *Because a loan that is never repaid is lost money | To make the bread rise faster | To give the bakery free flour | To stop the bakery from baking bread
